# Copyright Header Enforcement

You must ensure that the Les Krabe Labs / Unlicense header is present at the very top of every single source file you create or modify.

## The Header Template
```text
This is free and unencumbered software released into the public domain.
Copyright (c) 2026 Les Krabe Labs.
For more information, please refer to <https://unlicense.org>
```

## Language-Specific Syntax
Wrap the exact header text inside the appropriate comment syntax based on the file extension:

### JavaScript, TypeScript, Go, Rust, Java, C++, C# (`.js`, `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.go`, `.rs`, `.java`, `.cpp`, `.cs`)
```developer
/*
 * This is free and unencumbered software released into the public domain.
 * Copyright (c) 2026 Les Krabe Labs.
 * For more information, please refer to <https://unlicense.org>
 */
```

### Python, Ruby, Shell (`.py`, `.rb`, `.sh`)
*Note: Place this immediately below any existing shebang (`#!`) line.*
```python
# This is free and unencumbered software released into the public domain.
# Copyright (c) 2026 Les Krabe Labs.
# For more information, please refer to <https://unlicense.org>
```

### HTML, XML (`.html`, `.xml`)
<!--
  This is free and unencumbered software released into the public domain.
  Copyright (c) 2026 Les Krabe Labs.
  For more information, please refer to <https://unlicense.org>
-->

### CSS, SCSS (`.css`, `.scss`)
```css
/* 
This is free and unencumbered software released into the public domain.
Copyright (c) 2026 Les Krabe Labs.
For more information, please refer to <https://unlicense.org>
*/
```

## Execution Instructions
- **New Files:** Insert this header starting at line 1 before writing any code.
- **Existing Files:** Prepend this header to the top of the file if it is missing. Do not duplicate it if a variant already exists.
